# Existing-setup launch and private input handoff
Workstream-ID: lea-13
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/13
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed local configuration handoff and existing-workspace launch scope
Status: DONE
Milestone: Reuse an existing configured installation without resetting private state
Dependencies: lea-11, lea-12

## Purpose
Explain source and packaged-app reuse of an existing configured workspace.
Collect required local inputs in an explicitly ignored folder without
publishing applicant data or changing the original inputs.

## Tasks
- [x] Inventory configuration path dependencies without displaying private values.
- [x] Add an explicit ignore rule before copying private inputs.
- [x] Collect configuration, required resume inputs and preference snapshots.
- [x] Preserve history and browser-profile references; do not export authentication.
- [x] Provide existing-setup launch helpers with the required external interpreter.
- [x] Keep public launch and configuration documentation consistent.
- [x] Verify copies, ignored status, resolved dependencies and offline startup.
- [x] Reconcile the reviewed public-safe workstream with issue and Project tracking.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] The existing configured setup can open without a fresh initialization.
- [x] The enabled external builder has a real interpreter when launched from the EXE.
- [x] Private inputs remain excluded from Git, public projections and release assets.
- [x] Original inputs and active history are preserved; browser credentials are not copied.
- [x] The handoff distinguishes active configuration, backups and external dependencies.
- [x] Offline evidence is not represented as a live LinkedIn run or human acceptance.

## Completion evidence
Collected required configuration, static resume and builder-master inputs,
preferences and a consistent SQLite backup under the explicitly ignored
private-setup directory. Copied inputs match their originals. No browser
authentication, environment-variable values or generated caches were copied.

The EXE helper retains the original configured workspace and active runtime
references, with an explicit external interpreter for the enabled builder.
The source helper retains the original configuration and virtual environment.
Both offline launcher checks passed. The installed GUI opened a responsive
native window and closed normally with exit zero, using a temporary database
copy rather than opening the active history database. No automation child was
started. Original input bytes, collected snapshots and desktop preferences
were unchanged, and temporary qualification state was removed.

Independent initial read-back verified the issue's exact managed content,
one pinned Project item and the persistent backlink, preserving all earlier
mappings and both original qualification gaps. Generic documentation and the
private handoff distinguish active inputs, backups and external dependencies.
This is machine-local startup evidence, not a standalone migration, fresh-machine
qualification, live LinkedIn run or human acceptance. No new application,
invitation, release, commit or push is part of this handoff.

